cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CTMS: Canonical Tool Manifest Specification"
message: "If you use this specification, please cite as below."
type: standard
authors:
  - given-names: George
    family-names: Kanellopoulos
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3162-1624"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gkanellopoulos/ctms"
url: "https://gkanellopoulos.github.io/ctms/"
abstract: >
  CTMS defines a signing and verification scheme for MCP (Model Context Protocol)
  tool metadata. It addresses tool description poisoning attacks by providing
  a canonical, signable representation of tool capabilities, keyless signing
  via Sigstore, in-toto attestation envelopes, and a client-side verification
  procedure. The signed artifact is a Sealed Tool Manifest (STM).
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - supply chain security
  - cryptographic attestation
  - tool integrity
  - Sigstore
  - in-toto
  - JCS
  - RFC 8785
  - AI security
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-06-10"
